    <docsection name="gcab-cabinet">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="libgcab/gcab-cabinet.c"
           line="27">A GCabCabinet is a handle to a Cabinet archive. It allows examining,
extracting and creation of archives.</doc>
    </docsection>
    <docsection name="gcab-file">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="libgcab/gcab-file.c"
           line="28">A GCabFile is a handle to a file inside a Cabinet archive.
It can either be a file that is already within an exisiting
archive, or a file that reference a file on disk that will be used
for a new archive creation. In the later case, gcab_file_get_file()
must return a valid handle.</doc>
    </docsection>
    <docsection name="gcab-folder">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="libgcab/gcab-folder.c"
           line="28">A GCabFolder is a handle to a folder within the Cabinet archive. A
Cabinet folder &lt;emphasis&gt;is not&lt;/emphasis&gt; like a directory. It is
a sub-container grouping GCabFiles together, sharing some common
settings like the compression method.

You can retrieve the files within a folder with
gcab_folder_get_files().

In order to add a file to a folder for creation, use
gcab_folder_add_file().</doc>
    </docsection>
  </namespace>
</repository>
